  "title": "Targeted retry arguments are Bun path filters, so the retry can run files that never failed",
  "detail": "Only names starting with '-' get a './' prefix. Bun treats any other relative argument as a substring filter over test paths. Reproduction (Bun 1.4.2): files a.test.ts, data.test.ts and test/a.test.ts; `bun test 'a.test.ts'` ran all 3 files, `bun test './a.test.ts'` ran 1. Codex reproduced the same with test/a.test.ts and other/test/a.test.ts: the bare form also ran the unrelated failing file and exited 1. So a targeted retry can confirm a failure in a file that passed in the original run, and the five-file bound for skipping the gate slot does not bound what actually runs. Fix: prefix every validated relative name with './' (keep the quoting), and add a test where a failing file name is a substring of another file's path."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": ".limitless.toml",
