  "title": "The targeted retry runs files without the per-file isolation the full check has",
  "detail": "The full check runs `bun test --parallel=...`, and `bun test --help` says --parallel implies --isolate (a fresh global object per file). The retry template `bun test {files}` runs every file in one shared global. Reproduction: two files that each read and then set globalThis.owner, expecting it unset first. `bun test --parallel=1 ./a.test.ts ./b.test.ts` passes both; `bun test ./a.test.ts ./b.test.ts` fails b (it sees a's value). A targeted retry of two or more files can therefore fail when the full check would pass. After the change that becomes a false regression with no full rerun. On the baseline it is worse: the base check stays failing, and a check that fails on base never blocks, so a real regression in that check is not blocking for the whole run. Codex reproduced that end to end: retryBaselineFailures kept the baseline failing, and compareGates then returned still_failing with blocking=false for a candidate failure. Fix: `retry_files = \"bun test --isolate {files}\"`, with a test that two files leaking a global pass in a targeted retry."
