  "detail": "The bypass checks the earlier JUnit duration (at most 60 s over at most 5 files), but the retry inherits the check's timeoutSec (1800 s here). A file that hangs on retry (an intermittent deadlock is a common flake) then runs outside the gate slot for up to 30 minutes, holding one of the two agentTestSlots that implementers' test runs share. The duration also comes from a report written by the run under test, so it is a hint, not a limit. Reproduction (Codex): parse a report with `<testsuite file=\"test/a.test.ts\" failures=\"1\" time=\"0\"/>`, then call retryRegressions; the runner receives targeted=true, skipGateSlot=true and the unchanged 1800 s timeout. Fix: when a retry skips the slot, cap its timeout at a small multiple of the bound (for example 2 x UNSLOTTED_RETRY_MAX_SECONDS). A targeted timeout already falls through to the slotted full retry, so the cap enforces the bound without losing the check. Apply it once, in retryFailures, so the baseline and regression paths share it. Add a test that the unslotted request carries the capped timeout and that a timeout leads to the full retry."
